## Control {{controlId}}: Terminate Network Connections Associated with Communications Sessions at End of Sessions or After Defined Inactivity Period

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization terminates network connections after defined periods of inactivity within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through Conditional Access session controls and device configuration policies managed by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Session Timeout Enforcement:**
{{caPoliciesTotalCount}} Conditional Access policies enforce session termination controls:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}){{#if sessionControls}}: Session controls enforce sign-in frequency and persistent browser restrictions{{/if}}
{{/each}}

Conditional Access sign-in frequency policies require re-authentication after defined inactivity periods, automatically terminating idle sessions to prevent unauthorized access to CUI resources.
{{else}}
Conditional Access session termination controls have not been configured. Session inactivity timeout relies on application-level defaults.
{{/if}}

{{#if deviceConfigurationsActive}}
**Endpoint Session Controls:**
{{deviceConfigurationsCount}} device configuration policies enforce screen lock and session timeout at the endpoint level, ensuring devices automatically lock after defined inactivity periods.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine Conditional Access sign-in frequency settings, persistent browser session configurations, device lock timeout policies, and session termination logs.

